 ## Overview
-Neural Geometric Level of Detail (NGLD) is a neural representation for implicit 3D shapes that uses a Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) to store learned feature vectors, enabling adaptive multi-level detail (LOD) and real-time rendering via sparse sphere tracing [S1]. It solves the prohibitive cost of rendering large neural Signed Distance Functions (SDFs) by decoupling geometric complexity from the neural network size; instead of a single large MLP, it uses small, shallow MLPs (decoders) that decode features aggregated from the SVO [S1]. Unlike [NeuS](6060-neus.md) which uses volumetric rendering, or [MLP Neural Fields](3854-mlp-neural-fields.md) which rely on dense sampling, NGLD enables real-time frame rates by querying only necessary LODs during traversal and blending SDF values for continuous LOD transitions [S1].
+Neural Geometric Level of Detail (NGLD) is a neural representation for implicit 3D shapes that uses a Sparse Voxel Octree (SVO) to store learned feature vectors, enabling adaptive multi-level detail (LOD) and real-time rendering via sparse sphere tracing [S1]. Unlike fixed-size neural networks (e.g., DeepSDF, FFN) or dense voxel grids, NGLD decouples geometric complexity from network size by storing features in a sparse octree and using small, shallow MLPs as decoders [S1]. This allows the representation to scale memory usage with geometric detail while maintaining constant inference cost per query, achieving state-of-the-art geometry reconstruction quality with real-time performance [S1].
 
 ## How it works
-**Inputs:**
-*   Query point $\mathbf{x} \in \mathbb{R}^3$ [S1].
-*   Target continuous LOD level $\tilde{L} \ge 1$ [S1].
-*   Trained parameters: MLP weights $\Theta = \{\theta_1, \dots, \theta_{L_{max}}\}$ and SVO feature vectors $\mathcal{Z}$ [S1].
+NGLD builds on [Neural and primitive-based representations](10-neural-and-primitive-based-representations.md) by replacing the single latent vector or dense grid with a sparse octree of features. It represents Signed Distance Functions (SDFs) using an SVO of learned feature vectors and small MLP decoders for each level of detail (LOD) [S1].
 
-**Outputs:**
-*   Signed distance value $\hat{d}_{\bar{L}}$ at the blended LOD [S1].
